        "original_id": "e2a028e1-bc8a-55d0-a85c-e8a954f5320f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eugene O'Neill, Russell Edson, Gus Edson, Brutus Jones\n- Works: The Emperor Jones\n- Roles: playwright, Nobel laureate in Literature, poet, novelist, writer, illustrator, cartoonist-screenwriter, Pullman porter, emperor\n\nFacts:\n- Eugene O'Neill was born on October 16, 1888, and he was an American playwright and Nobel laureate in Literature.\n- The Emperor Jones is a 1920 play by American dramatist Eugene O'Neill.\n- In The Emperor Jones, Brutus Jones is a resourceful, self-assured African American and former Pullman porter who kills another black man in a dice game, is jailed, escapes, and sets himself up as emperor on a small backward Caribbean island.\n- Russell Edson was born in 1935, and he was an American poet, novelist, writer, and illustrator.\n- Russell Edson was the son of Gus Edson, who was a cartoonist-screenwriter.\n- Eugene O'Neill died on November 27, 1953.\n- Russell Edson died on April 29, 2014.",
